WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.501
-Thank you for being here
in person.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.934
The last time you were very nice
to us and you zoomed.

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:06.801
-I zoomed from my apartment,
and I was wearing sweatpants.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:08.400
-Oh, yeah, but I didn't know.
-Below.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.400
-I was wearing a Chanel jacket,
but, you know,

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.067
underneath it
was a sad situation.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.834
-Yeah.
Are you still living in London?

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:15.400
Or are you back living
in New York?

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.234
-I was living in London,
then I moved home

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:22.400
back with my parents up until
about a week ago.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.634
-No.
-And now I live here --

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:28.000
-Uh-huh.
-For a month, and then I go

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.701
to wherever --
-To other movies and things.

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:30.834
-Yes. Yes, yes.

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.000
-So you really don't really
have a home.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.267
-I don't have a home.
-No.

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.234
You're just traveling
and just being everywhere.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.801
And right now,
I don't have a job either.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:38.067
So I'm --

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.667
-[Laughing] Oh, my gosh.
-I'm looking for something.

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.434
-Wow. You were telling me
backstage

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.234
you have a new obsession.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:44.801
What is this?

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.200
-Formula 1.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:51.868
I don't know if it's, like,
a big thing here yet.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:54.167
But In Europe, it's --
-Massive.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.167
-It's massive.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.300
-No, in America, it is big.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.434
But I don't know in New York
if it's that big.

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:01.033
-Well --
-Is it?

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.200
-Yeah, New York, I don't know.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.200
-I don't know if it --
-Yeah, New Yorkers,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.200
we take our time.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.334
We go, "Well, we're not sure."

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:06.968
-Well, I'm going to make you all
get into it.

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.367
-Okay. Tell us.
School us.

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:11.434
So, there's this show on Netflix
called "Drive to Survive."

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:13.934
During the pandemic I didn't
really do anything, obviously,

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.334
like everyone else.
-Yeah.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.701
-But I watched this show,
and now --

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:20.400
-"Drive to Survive"?
-"Drive to Survive," on Netflix.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.400
It follows all the drivers,
the Formula 1 drivers.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.234
I never cared about sports
before, by the way.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.267
And now, I'm completely hooked.

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:29.667
They're all gorgeous.

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:30.868
-Yeah.
-It's like --

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.701
it's like a boy band
kind of thing.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.601
You follow their lives.

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:37.667
Also, one of the team
principals, the boss

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.667
of Red Bull, is married
to Geri Horner,

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.367
who's a Spice Girl.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:43.734
-Oh, yeah, Geri.
-So, that's --

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:44.968
There's something for everyone.

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:46.901
-Yeah.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.501
-And it's really fun.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:53.300
And so -- actually, Brad Pitt
is making a Formula 1 movie.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.300
[ Cheers ]

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.467
-Yeah.

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:59.834
-And I have the same manager
as Brad Pitt.

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.868
Flex.

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:03.267
-Okay, now we're --
now we're getting somewhere.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:06.000
-So, I was at dinner with my
manager, and I was obviously

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.300
talking about it.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.067
And she was like, "Oh, he's
making a movie about it."

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.400
And I was like, "Get Brad Pitt
on the phone right now."

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.334
And she called him.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.501
-She did?

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.667
-And I said, "I will do anything
in this movie.

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:21.601
I will have one line,
I will be in the pit crew,

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:23.734
I will do whatever you want."
-Yeah.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.534
-But I've got to be
in this film.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.067
-And -- And I am obsessed with
Formula 1, yeah.

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:30.133
-Obsessed.
And he said, "I'm such a fan.

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:32.400
I watched 'Behind Her Eyes'
twice.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.734
You're in it, kid."

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:34.734
-What?!

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:37.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:39.567
That's how you -- that's how
you make stuff happen.

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:41.200
-Yeah.
-Wow!

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.267
Do we know where
and how you're in it?

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:44.734
-I have no clue.
-No.

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:46.100
-I have no clue.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.567
But I feel like we had a verbal
agreement over the phone,

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:51.267
and if you say it on national
television, it's legally binded.

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:52.601
-It's legal.
Yes, that is correct.

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:55.334
We have lawyers here that will
say that it is legal.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:56.934
Yeah.
-So, that's fine.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:59.868
So, if I'm not in that movie,
give him hell the next time --

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:01.300
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.067
All right, I'm going to be into
both of those things.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.567
I want to talk about
"Bad Sisters,"

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:06.000
which I'm totally into,
by the way.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.901
-Yay.
-It's great, it's fantastic,

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:10.200
it's a good plot.
I love the whole idea of it.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.634
You shot it in Ireland.
-Mm-hm.

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:13.734
-You scared me when you jumped
off that cliff, by the way.

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:14.968
-I know. I scared everyone
when I did that.

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.100
-Yeah.
You don't have to do that stuff.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.300
-I know. That's what
the stunt people told me,

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:23.467
but I was preparing to jump into
the water and my friend who does

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:26.234
it everyday -- it's kind of an
Irish thing, that we jump into

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:27.834
Irish Sea and --

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:29.734
It's to get over your hangover,
basically.

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:30.901
-Oh, there you go.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.434
Now I know
what you're talking about.

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:33.567
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:36.534
And when we got to actually
shoot the scene,

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:39.334
they just asked me
to jump off the steps.

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:43.200
And I was like, "Oh, no, no, no,
no, no, I've been scaring the...

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.300
out of myself every weekend
to do this."

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.367
So, I asked them if I could jump
off the cliff.

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:50.467
-Yeah.
-Yeah, in Dublin.

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.734
And here you go.
Look at this.

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.400
Rebel without a cause,
right there.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.868
Just jumping off.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.133
Scaring everyone.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:58.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:00.601
-But that's you putting your all
into --

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:01.968
-I know, I was like
"We're making a TV show."

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.033
-That's the type of stuff
that they need in

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:04.567
that Formula 1 movie
with Brad Pitt.

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.701
You'll be jumping off stuff.
Yeah, exactly.

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:08.501
-I don't know if they jump in
Formula 1,

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:09.868
but I'll make it happen.

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:11.467
-This driver does.

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:14.167
You jump into your car.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:17.634
-But, can we explain what
"Bad Sisters," the plot of this?

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:19.801
And congrats on the great
reviews, by the way.

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:20.834
Well-deserved.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.167
-I think one of the reviews
said,

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:26.434
"It's the Avengers
assembles of Irish talent."

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:29.601
-Yeah! That's exact--
not too shabby, right there.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:32.133
-I was like, "Oh, I like that."
-Yeah, I love it.

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.734
I like that it starts off --
Well, you explain it

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.033
and then I'll tell you
what I like about it.

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:40.133
-Okay. So it's about
five Irish sisters

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:44.000
who hate one of their sisters'
husbands.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.834
-And he's the worst.
-Because he is the worst.

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:47.601
-He is the worst.
-He is a terrible,

00:04:47.601 --> 00:04:49.133
despicable human being.
-Yes.

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:52.534
-And so, they decide
to kill him.

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:53.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:56.801
And they have absolutely
no business being murderers.

00:04:56.801 --> 00:04:57.801
They're terrible at it.

00:04:57.801 --> 00:04:58.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:02.267
And there is all these awful
failed attempts.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:05.167
And you know he's dead
from the first episode.

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:06.501
-That's what I was going to say.
I like that.

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.033
'Cause you don't have to go,
"Oh, are they going --"

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.434
He's dead.
-He's dead.

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:11.567
-Someone killed him.
-It opens with his funeral.

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:15.434
And then -- but you just
don't know who did it.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.300
-It's well done.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.067
Here's Eve Hewson
in "Bad Sisters."

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.133
Take a look at this.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:22.567
-I want in.

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:26.033
I want to help.

00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:28.067
-No.

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:32.300
No way.
-You're pushing me out, Eva.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.534
You're not being my mom,
or my sister, or my friend.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.234
-Yeah, well fine if I'm not
being any of those things,

00:05:37.234 --> 00:05:38.801
but I'm not going to stop
protecting you --

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:40.367
-You're not protecting me!
-Because that is my job.

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:42.067
-You're isolating me.
-I don't even know why

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:45.300
I'm having to --

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:49.367
What we're doing is really,
really bad.

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:52.534
-No, it's not.

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:56.267
It's survival.

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:59.467
Someone's not coming out
the other side of this.

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:02.868
And it's not going to be me.

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:05.334
And it sure as [bleep] is not
going to be one of my sisters.

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:06.334
-Yeah!

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:07.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.901
"Bad Sisters" assemble!
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:12.367
Eve Hewson, everybody.

00:06:12.367 --> 00:06:16.300
"Bad Sisters" premieres
this Friday on Apple TV plus.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:18.033
Fallon Book Club author
Gabrielle Zevin

00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:19.968
joins us after the break.
Stick around, everybody.

